LeetCode 993 — Cousins in Binary Tree
1. Problem Statement

You are given a binary tree and two node values x and y.

You need to determine whether x and y are cousins.

Two nodes are cousins if:

They are at the same depth.
They have different parents.
Example
        1
       / \
      2   3
     /     \
    4       5

For:

x = 4
y = 5

Depth:

4 → depth 2
5 → depth 2

Parents:

parent(4) = 2
parent(5) = 3

Different parents + same depth:

4 and 5 → cousins

Answer:

true
2. 🧠 Your Intuition

You divided the problem into two independent checks.

Check 1 — Same depth

You use:

int depth1 = depth(root, x, 1);
int depth2 = depth(root, y, 1);

Your depth() recursively searches for the node and returns its depth.

Then:

depth1 == depth2

means:

x and y are at the same level.

Check 2 — Not siblings

Your check() function looks at every parent.

For example:

        2
       / \
      4   5

If:

x = 4
y = 5

then:

root.left.val == x
root.right.val == y

So they are children of the same parent.

That means they are siblings, not cousins.

Therefore:

return false;


Logic :

Find the depth of both nodes and make sure they are equal, then traverse the tree and make sure x and y are never the left and right children of the same parent.


Code:

class Solution {
    public boolean isCousins(TreeNode root, int x, int y) {
        int depth1=depth(root,x,1);
        int depth2=depth(root,y,1);
        return check(root,x,y) && depth1==depth2 ;
    }
    boolean check(TreeNode root,int x,int y){
         if(root==null){
            return true;
        }
        if(root.val==x || root.val==y){
            return true;
        }
        if((root.left!=null && root.right!=null) && (root.left.val==x && root.right.val==y ||root.left.val==y && root.right.val==x )){
            return false;
        }
        return check(root.left,x,y) && check(root.right,x,y);

    }
    
     int depth(TreeNode node,int nodeval,int num){
        if(node==null){
            return 0;
        }
        if(node.val==nodeval){
            return num;
        }
        int ans1=depth(node.left,nodeval,num+1);
        int ans2=depth(node.right,nodeval,num+1);
        
        return ans1>=ans2?ans1:ans2;

    }
    }
